Login shell here is Nushell, and Emacs inherits it: without this,
`shell-file-name' becomes nu and scripted callers break — dired
calls `\ls --dired', which nu neither parses nor flags. So scripted
processes get POSIX sh while interactive `M-x shell' keeps nu.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(setq shell-file-name "/bin/sh"
      explicit-shell-file-name "/usr/local/bin/nu")
#+end_src
